+.. _cli_import_resumable:
+
+Resumable NDJSON imports
+=======================
+
+``import-resumable`` imports an immutable local UTF-8 NDJSON file and records a
+durable checkpoint with each batch:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils import-resumable events.db events events.ndjson \
+        --import-id daily-2026-09-13 --pk id --batch-size 100 --alter
+
+Run the same command after interruption to continue from committed progress.
+Successful output is a JSON object containing ``import_id``, ``rows_committed``,
+``byte_offset`` and ``completed``. Expected failures print ``Error:`` and exit
+nonzero. Repeat ``--pk`` for compound keys; ``--upsert`` updates matching keys and
+``--alter`` permits new columns. Batch size defaults to 100 and may change on
+resume. Source bytes, destination and insertion options must otherwise match the
+ID's existing metadata, including when the import has completed.
+
+LF/CRLF, blank lines, a leading UTF-8 BOM and a final object without a newline
+are accepted. Malformed or incomplete final records fail their batch. Correcting
+or appending to the file changes its identity and cannot silently resume under
+the same ID. Stdin, views and virtual tables are not supported.
+
+Rows, schema changes and each checkpoint commit together. See
+:ref:`the Python API <python_api_resumable_import>` for metadata and recovery
+details, and for post-commit progress callbacks.
+
