+.. _python_api_resumable_import:
+
+Resuming a local NDJSON import
+=============================
+
+Use ``table.insert_file_resumable()`` when a large import must continue after
+interruption without repeating committed rows:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    db = Database("events.db")
+    state = db["events"].insert_file_resumable(
+        "events.ndjson", import_id="daily-2026-09-13", pk="id",
+        batch_size=100, alter=True, upsert=False, progress=print,
+    )
+
+The result and progress notifications contain ``import_id``, ``rows_committed``,
+``byte_offset`` and ``completed``. Counts are cumulative source objects, including
+objects that update existing keys. Progress callbacks run after the checkpoint
+commits; their exceptions propagate without undoing that checkpoint. Notifications
+are independent dictionaries. A trailing-whitespace or empty-file checkpoint may
+contain no new objects. Completed imports return immediately without callbacks.
+
+Files must be immutable, regular local UTF-8 NDJSON files containing one JSON
+object per nonblank line. A leading BOM, CRLF/LF, Unicode and a final object without
+a newline are accepted. Incomplete JSON, scalar/array records and NaN/Infinity are
+errors. Input is streamed one batch at a time, after a full-file SHA-256 scan.
+Empty files complete without requiring creation of the destination table.
+
+Metadata is stored in ``_sqlite_utils_imports``, keyed by ``import_id``. Its
+``table_name``, ``source_sha256``, ``options_json``, ``byte_offset``,
+``rows_committed`` and ``completed`` columns describe identity and durable progress.
+The options JSON contains ``pk`` (list or null), ``alter`` and ``upsert``.
+Do not edit this metadata or use its table as an import destination.
+
+Reusing an ID requires identical source bytes, destination table and insertion
+options, even after completion. Moving the identical file or changing batch size
+is allowed. A single PK name is equivalent to a one-element sequence. Mismatches
+raise ``ValueError`` before mutation. Repaired or appended bytes are a different
+source and cannot silently reuse the same ID. Views and virtual tables are not
+supported.
+
+Each batch's rows, newly created table or columns and progress update share one
+transaction. Failures roll back the whole current batch, including insertion
+sub-batches and trigger side effects; previous checkpoints remain committed.
+Reopen the database and call the method with the same ID to resume. The method
+rejects an existing caller transaction with ``TransactionError`` because its
+checkpoints must commit durably. Concurrent source edits, external metadata/data
+changes and concurrent import workers are outside this interface's contract.
+
+The equivalent CLI is :ref:`import-resumable <cli_import_resumable>`.
+
